fix:
Wrap the validated construct in a dedicated type with a private inner value and a smart constructor.
```rust
pub struct EmailAddress(String);

impl EmailAddress {
    pub fn new(email: String) -> Result<Self, String> {
        if email.contains('@') { // simplified check
            Ok(EmailAddress(email))
        } else {
            Err("Invalid email format".into())
        }
    }
}
